  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday morning through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 211 PM EDT Wed Aug 5 2026\n\nThe models are in good agreement with the long term weather pattern, \nwhich is characterized by a more prominent Bermuda High and \nrising heights over the extended period. The CWA will remain along\nthe periphery of this high pressure supporting a general \nsoutherly flow and a continuation of elevated PWATs ranging from \n1.5-2\". This setup will reinforce the summertime pattern with weak\nflow aloft and a stricter diurnal distribution of isolated to \nscattered pulse-type thunderstorms as we approach the weekend. PoP\nchances will remain in the 30-60% range over the area through the\nfirst of next week. Some of the storms may become strong with \ngusty winds and localized flash flooding considerations. This \npattern will support a general downward trend in cloud cover and \nan upward trend in temperatures, rising slightly into the upper \n80s to low 90s outside of mountain areas by the weekend. As \nconditions warm, the potential for triple- digit heat indices will\nincrease, and we will keep an eye on the possibility of issuing a\nHeat Advisory.",
